Account Setup

I set up IAM Identity Center with a permission set for my user account with admin access, and I turned on MFA for it. The root user is not used for daily work.

I made a separate IAM user called scanner just for this project, so the scanner never runs with admin rights.

I set up a CloudTrail trail that logs management events (read and write) in all regions. The logs are encrypted with a KMS key, log file validation is on, and they go to S3 and CloudWatch Logs.

I'm adding CloudWatch alarms for root account usage and EC2 launches, plus an AWS Budgets alert if my spending goes over $2.

Why I set it up this way

I wanted to separate my own access from the scanner's access, log everything that happens in the account, and get alerted when something unusual happens. 
I turned on management events only, not data events, because data events cost extra and this is a personal account.
